{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the Canaanite heard.</b> He heard that Aaron had died and the clouds of glory had departed, etc., as is stated in Rosh Hashanah (3a) — and Amalek has always been a strap of chastisement for Israel, ready at all times for punishment." "<b>Dweller of the Negev.</b> This is Amalek, as it says: ״עֲמָלֵק יוֹשֵׁב בְּאֶרֶץ הַנֶּגֶב״ (Numbers 13). He changed his language to speak in the Canaanite tongue, so that Israel would pray to the Holy One, blessed be He, to deliver the Canaanites into their hand — but they are not Canaanites. Israel saw their garments like the garments of Amalekites and their tongue the Canaanite tongue. They said: let us pray without specification, as it says: ״אִם נָתֹן תִּתֵּן אֶת הָעָם הַזֶּה בְּיָדִי״." "<b>The way of the Atharim.</b> The way of the Negev, by which the spies went, as it says: ״וַיַּעֲלוּ בַנֶּגֶב״ (Numbers 13). Another interpretation: דֶּרֶךְ הָאֲתָרִים — the way of the spy, the great one who travels before them, as it says (ibid. 10): ״דֶּרֶךְ שְׁלֹשֶׁת יָמִים לָתוּר לָהֶם מְנוּחָה״ (Tanhuma)." "<b>And he took from it captives.</b> This was only one maidservant."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:53.621299159Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}